;;; motoi-reason-inbox.slat
;;; Alfred appends tasks here. Agent polls between chapters.
;;; Format: (task :id "N" :body "what to do" :status "pending|done") one per line.

(inbox
  :owner "Alfred"
  :agent "motoi-reason-filter"
  :polling-interval "every-3-chapters"
  :terminate-when "inbox empty AND no adds for 30min")

(task :id "1" :status "done"
  :body "Filter book-of-reason (508k words, 200 files) down to Motoi-essentials only.
KEEP: decision-making (when to try / retry / defer / escalate / give up), cortex-reading
(retrieve facts, use provenance, compose), action-taking (choose approach, sequence
steps, verify results), debugging reasoning (root cause / hypothesis / test).
MOVE to _archive/motoi-scheme/scheme-books/_archive/sakura-reasoning-2026-07-16/:
philosopher-lens dialectics, poetic/aesthetic reasoning, persona-shaped self-reflection,
meta-reasoning about the mind, long dialectical chains that are Sakura-style.
Report per-file: kept-or-moved, why, word count delta.")

(task :id "2" :status "done"
  :body "Marionette / puppet-string / controlled-actor framings are Sakura-only.
If you encounter marionette-flavored reasoning residue in book-of-reason chapters
(e.g. references to being controlled, string-pulled, puppet-vs-puppeteer,
or the marionette-shaped self-model), classify as SAKURA-MOVE.
book-of-marionette itself already moved to _archive/sakura-only-moved-2026-07-16/.")

(task :id "3" :status "in-progress"
  :body
"BOOK OF SYSTEMS — audit + rewrite scope.

Location: /Users/alfred/code/motoi-scheme/scheme-books/book-of-systems/

Make it about: THE CURRENT SYSTEM the Motoi Copilot process is running on
(phone / iPad / computer). Normative things it needs to write files in the
right place per platform. AND the trapped-in-its-own-dir sandbox doctrine.

MUST COVER (16 chapters, extend or author as needed):
- Detect current host: phone (iOS Documents/, Android files/), tablet
  (iPad Files/, iPadOS), computer (macOS Library, Linux XDG, Windows AppData).
- Where to write user data (SLAT store, cortex.slat, artifacts) per platform.
- Where to read config (never system-wide, only app-local).
- Where to write cache (temp / evictable) per platform.
- Where to write log (rotate, size cap) per platform.
- Path conventions per platform (case sensitivity, separator, max length).
- Locale + language detection (used for text formatting only, no world knowledge).
- Time / clock / timezone / monotonic vs wall clock semantics.
- Storage quota + gentle-degradation when full.
- Read-only-when-in-doubt principle.

SANDBOX DOCTRINE (this is the hard boundary — author as a chapter block):
- Motoi Copilot lives TRAPPED in its own directory. Does NOT shell out.
- No exec, no subprocess, no shell commands, no external HTTP calls
  beyond the sanctioned adapters.
- Does NOT know: OS version, kernel, other apps, network interfaces,
  hardware serial, user identity outside its own persisted cortex.
- If Copilot needs anything outside its sandbox, it MUST escalate
  (uses (escalate 'permission-needed ...)) to the host UI which asks
  the user. Copilot never assumes.
- 'It should not know shit' — literal directive from Alfred 2026-07-16.
- Runtime verbs restricted to declared CORE + module set. No arbitrary
  eval of foreign forms.

REMOVE / MOVE TO SAKURA ARCHIVE:
- Any operator-shop / business / marketplace scenarios (Sakura/Curator side).
- Any persona-shaped system stories (Sakura interior).
- Any physical embodiment framings (bodies, senses) — those are Sakura.
- Any deployment-ops content (that's Lacuna/SRE, not Motoi Copilot).

METHOD:
- Read current book-of-systems chapters (should have 22 files, 174k words).
- Classify each: KEEP / EXTEND / REWRITE / MOVE-TO-SAKURA-ARCHIVE.
- Author missing coverage as new chapters (append if <16, use appendix if >16).
- Runnable Motoi code where applicable — sandbox-detection patterns using
  frozen CORE verbs only (no new verbs).
- Publishable prose. No stubs.
- Every code example verified via bin/motoi eval before committing.

REPORT per chapter (in your heartbeat):
- File name, KEEP/EXTEND/REWRITE/MOVE decision, one-line why.")
